      "writtenOn": "2026-03-30T16:30:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Maybe I wasn\u0027t too clear with that :)\n\nSo if I had this defined as a regex_replace in blob fixups and I wanted to add another subhal, I\u0027d have to update the blob fixups to include it (one commit), re-run extraction and then do another commit on the vendor tree afterwards.\n\nIf I had hals.conf in the device tree in the first place, adding a new subhal would only need a change in the device tree (assuming that of course, the subhal I\u0027m adding isn\u0027t also blobbed).\n\nSo yes, I still think it makes more sense to have it in the device tree in case I\u0027m going to need another subhal in the future.",
